-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",340,{
[10849]="7002D5F8\n1\tA scent of evil draws you deep into the Trollshaws\tYou are drawn to a source of evil detected in the Trollshaws by your keen senses. If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.\n2\tDestroy a scrap of black armour\030Destroy a scrap of black cloth\tTrophies of the evil steed can be found in the area where it met its death. If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.\n3\tExamine the fallen black steed once more\tThe trophies left behind by the fallen black steed and its rider have been destroyed. With your rage satisfied, curiosity has crept in. What could have killed this steed, and where was its rider going?\n4\tFind the source of that which drove the black steed away\tA powerful force left a mysterious energy about the black steed's corpse, like a receeding wave would leave small pools of water to linger in the sand. The black steed did not make it far after suffering an injury so great. The source of such a power must exist somewhere in the Trollshaws.\n",
[10850]="7002D5F7\n1\tHead to Ost Guruth and find a horse there\tThere is a horse in Ost Guruth that you feel compelled to seek out. If defeated or time expires, you will return to the Horsefields.\n2\tDefeat ambushing crebain (total: 3)\tThe rare herb sought by Radagast's horse only grows in places of high elevation. The only place high enough for miles around Ost Guruth is the summit of Weathertop. If defeated or time expires, you will return to the Horsefields.\n3\tTake the herbs back to Radagast's horse\tRadagast's horse is found in Ost Guruth. If defeated or time expires, you will return to the horsefields.\n",
[10851]="70072140\n1\tEavesdrop on your husband's conversation\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should approach Góramul Sai and listen to the conversation.\n2\tTalk to your husband\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should talk to Góramul Sai in the banquet hall.\n3\tListen to the conversation\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should hear what Dark Priestess Barkhuráni has to say to Góramul Sai.\n4\tTalk to your sister\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should talk to Dark Priestess Barkhuráni in the banquet hall.\n5\tCheck on your son\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should find Otibúk in the southern bed-chamber.\n6\tUse your Icy Glare on Ratúlko\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should use Icy Glare on Ratúlko the Bloody to let him know how you feel.\n7\tCheck on your son\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should find Otibúk in the southern bed-chamber.\n8\tCheck on your daughters\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should find your daughters in the northern bed-chamber.\n9\tFind Khêjiba in the central garden\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should find Khêjiba. She is hiding somewhere in the royal living quarters.\n10\tTalk to Lokóya\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should return Khêjiba to the northern bed-chamber.\n11\tFind your husband\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should find Góramul Sai in your shared bed-chamber, to the rear of the living quarters.\n12\tUse your Diplomatic Words to convince your husband\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should use your Diplomatic Words to convince Góramul Sai to leave.\n13\tListen to your husband's words\tYou are experiencing Kotráka Saiya's story from her point of view. You should hear Góramul Sai's response.\n",
[10852]="70008772\n1\tReturn to Gazlup at Lugazag\030Collect fragments of troll-stone (total: 5)\030Collect slabs of troll-stone (total: 5)\tSoldier Gazlup is at Lugazag. Soldier Gazlup directed you to collect troll-stone to repair the damage the trolls delivered to the walls of Lugazag.\n",
[10853]="70017584\n1\tDefeat Drâgh\tDrâgh can be found at the Grand Stair, east from the Redhorn Lodes and north-west from the Shadowed Refuge in the Foundations of Stone. You should defeat Drâgh at the Grand Stair to prevent his further interference with the dwarf expedition in Moria.\n2\tReturn to Armbeald at the Redhorn Lodes\tArmbeald can be found at the Orc-Watch in north-west of the Redhorn Lodes. You should return to Armbeald and tell him that Drâgh has been defeated through the efforts of you and your friends.\n",
[10854]="70061CCC\n1\tSpeak with Akúlhun at Gramsfoot\tSpeak with War-tyrant Akúlhun about available tasks.\n",
[10855]="7004CE44\n1\tDefeat Esgaroth smugglers (total: 10)\tEsgaroth smugglers can be found in Esgaroth-of-old. You should defeat Esgaroth smugglers.\n2\tTalk to Mervárth\tMervárth can be found outside Esgaroth-of-old. You should talk to Mervárth.\n",
[10856]="7002731E\n1\tPlace the three snap-jaw traps near the footprints until you have used them up (total: 3)\030Find a suitable place to set the traps near the footprints\tYou found footprints on the far shore of the lake, north-west of the eyot and beneath the cliffs west of the shore, and now Wynfor wants you to set three traps he made at those locations. Wynfor has given you three traps he has made, and he wants you to set them in the vicinity of the footprints you found earlier.\n2\tYou have placed the snap-jaw traps in Tâl Methedras, as Wynfor wanted.\t\n3\tTalk to Wynfor at Tûr Morva\tWynfor is in Tûr Morva. You have set the traps for Wynfor and should now return to him.\n",
[10857]="7002D340\n1\tCollect dull blades (total: 6)\tDull blades can be found on weapon-racks in the North Wing of Durin's Threshold. You should collect several dull blades for restoration in the newly-lit forge.\n2\tUse the forge to restore the blades (total: 6)\tThe forge of the North Wing can be found near Athils. You should use the forge to restore the blades you collected.\n3\tBring the new-restored blades to Athils\tAthils is in the North Wing of Durin's Threshold, overseeing the work being done there. You should bring the newly restored blades to Athils.\n",
[10858]="70044D54\n1\tTalk to Gord Dunley\tGord Dunley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith. Gord Dunley has voiced concerns about performing in the Stone Theatre and Polla has asked you to investigate.\n2\tTalk to Polla Stoutley\tPolla Stoutley can be found just outside the Stone Theatre in Minas Tirith. Gord Dunley has requested that the band perform in another space as he feels his voice is lacking in the Stone Theatre.\n3\tMeet the Cloudyheads at the Hall of Air\tThe Hall of Air can be found in the northern section of the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith. Polla is displeased, but willing to try a different theatre at Gord's request. You should meet the Cloudyheads at the Hall of Air.\n4\tTalk to Polla Stoutley in the Hall of Air\tPolla Stoutley can be found in the Hall of Air in the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith. You have arrived at the Hall of Air and should now talk to Polla.\n5\tTalk to Hollur\tHollur can be found in the Hall of Air. Polla has asked you to speak to Hollur about testing the theatre's acoustics.\n6\tThe Hall of Air can be found in the Fifth Circle. Polla Stoutley has asked you to sit in various seats in the Hall of Air to help Hollur ensure that the sound is even throughout the theatre.\t\n7\tTalk to Hollur\tHollur can be found in the Hall of Air. You have tested various seats in the theatre and much to your dismay, it seems there is a wide range of quality in the available seating.\n8\tTalk to Robbo Gristback\tRobbo Gristback is in the Hall of Air in Minas Tirith. Hollur has asked you to speak to Robbo about an idea he had on the way to the Hall of Air.\n9\tOrnate instruments can be found at various markets in Minas Tirith. Robbo Gristback hopes to purchase instruments of finer make to help his band put on a better show in Minas Tirith. He has provided the gold and has asked you to peruse the markets of the City.\t\n10\tDeliver the instruments to Robbo Gristback\tRobbo Gristback can be found in the Hall of Air in the Fifth Circle of Minas Tirith. You have acquired several new instruments for the Cloudyheads and should now deliver them to Robbo.\n11\tTalk to Polla Stoutley\tPolla Stoutley can be found in Hall of Air. You have delivered the instruments to Robbo in the Hall of Air. Robbo has informed you that Polla would like to talk to you.\n",
[10859]="7006C57B\n1\tPost the inciting letter outside of the Ordâkhai camp north of Jirush\tAmalíbi provided the notice and a sounding horn and asked you to make your way to the Ordâkhai camp north of Jirush. You need to find a suitable location to post the notice and then find a suitable place to hide, and blow the horn.\n2\tUse the sounding horn when you are concealed from the front gate\030Conceal yourself from view\tYou posted the inciting letter. You should retreat to a location concealed from the entrance and blow the sounding horn to draw a guard to gate.\n3\tReturn to Amalíbi with news from the Ordâkhai encampment\tA soldier emerged from the camp, took the note, and immediately called for Jombahok. Return to Amalíbi at Ghalbûru and tell her of the success.\n",
[10860]="7000978C\n1\tUse Rock\030Defeat Bonefang\tThe wolf camp can be found north-east of Oatbarton. Now that you have brought him the elk-meat, Hal Gamgee suggests that it is time to lay the trap for the big wolf by placing the meat outside of the wolf's cave.\n2\tTalk to Hal Gamgee\030Collect Elk-meat\tHal Gamgee is in Oatbarton centre. You should return to Hal Gamgee with news of your victory.\n",
[10861]="70007043\n1\tDefeat Hontimûrz\030Defeat Hontimûrz's guards (total: 4)\tNaerost lies just east of Weathertop, north of Hunulf Munce. Hunulf Munce is concerned that the half-orcs are servants of a greater power, perhaps even Mordor. He has asked you to enter Naerost and defeat their leader and his guards in hopes that the rest will flee.\n2\tTalk to Hunulf Munce\tHunulf Munce awaits your return at his camp on the east side of Minas Eriol, south of Naerost. Though the half-orcs did not flee, their leader and his guards have been defeated. You should return to Hunulf Munce with the news.\n",
[10862]="70044581\n1\tTalk to the mysterious woman\tThe Old Guest-house lies in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. The mysterious woman stands before the Old Guest-house, talking to Bergil.\n2\tReturn to the breach in the cisterns\tYou can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle. The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further.\n3\tGather stones (total: 6)\tYou can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle. The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further. You should gather nearby stones for the task.\n4\tBlock up the breach\tYou can enter the cisterns at the southern end of the First Circle. The mysterious woman has bade you repair the breach where the goblins entered the cisterns before you speak further. Use the stones you've gathered to block up the hole.\n5\tTalk to Bergil\tThe breach is within the cisterns, which can be entered at the southern end of the First Circle. Bergil has come up just as you finished blocking up the breach.\n6\tLady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place. Bergil wants to take you to Lady Raenemel's house.\t\n7\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel is at her house in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place. You have found Lady's Raenemel's house and she is outside. Now you should talk to her.\n8\tStep away from Lady Raenemel's House\tLady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place. Lady Raenemel wishes to speak with you alone.\n9\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place. Lady Raenemel wishes to speak with you alone... outside her home.\n10\tStroll with Lady Raenemel\tStroll to the garden near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\n11\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated. Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.\n12\tStroll with Lady Raenemel\tStroll up onto the wall near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\n13\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated. Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.\n14\tStroll with Lady Raenemel\tContinue to stroll up on the wall near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\n15\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated. Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.\n16\tStroll with Lady Raenemel\tWalk to the fountain by the Baths near Lady Raenemel's home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\n17\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated. Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.\n18\tReturn to Raenemel's home\tReturn with Lady Raenemel to her home in the northern half of the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel will stroll with you around her neighbourhood. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated.\n19\tTalk to Lady Raenemel\tLady Raenemel will accompany you within the Fourth Circle of the City. Use the small whistle to call her, if you get separated. Talk to Lady Raenemel and see what she has to say next.\n20\tReturn to Lady Raenemel's house\tLady Raenemel's house is in the Fourth Circle, near the Finding Place. You should follow Lady Raenemel back to her house.\n21\tTalk to Bergil\tBergil stands outside Lady Raenemel's house in the Fourth Circle. Lady Raenemel and Bergil were speaking as you approached. Now Bergil seems to have something to say to you.\n",
[10863]="7001A4A9\n1\tDefeat Morsharpat at Ashúrz Maufulug\tMorsharpat is at Ashúrz Maufulug, south and a little west from Echad Glamodúd. Glamodúd has asked you to defeat Morsharpat, the captain of the Orcs at Ashúrz Maufulug.\n2\tTalk to Glamodúd at Echad Glamodúd\tGlamodúd is at Echad Glamodúd, north and a little east from Ashúrz Maufulug. You should return to Glamodúd with news of your victory against Morsharpat.\n",
[10864]="70052F9A\n1\tExplore Kidzul-kâlah\tKidzul-kâlah can be found alongside the Gladdenmere. You should destroy shadow sources and defeat any foes you find at Kidzul-kâlah.\n2\tDefeat foes at Kidzul-kâlah (total: 15)\030Destroy sources of shadow at Kidzul-kâlah (total: 10)\tKidzul-kâlah can be found alongside the Gladdenmere. You should destroy shadow sources and defeat any foes you find at Kidzul-kâlah.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many foes at Kidzul-kâlah.\n",
[10865]="7005278F\n1\tTalk to one of the hunters in Hultvís\tOne of the hunters from the village of Hultvís may know what has disturbed the shades in the Gladden Fields.\n2\tDefeat Orcs at Avabárg (total: 6)\tEurik asked you to defeat the Orcs he encountered at Avabárg while you search for his son.\n3\tDefeat shades on the Gladden Fields (total: 6)\tEurik believed that you might find his son among the shades of the Gladden Fields if you did not find him with the Orcs of Avabárg.\n4\tWhat is that noise?\tYou hear a faint voice calling from the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields!\n5\tLook for Badwila in the north-west of the Gladden Fields\tBadwila disappeared somewhere in the north-western reaches of the Gladden Fields.\n6\tTalk to Badwila among the Orc corpses\tYou have found Eurik's son Badwila. He has been injured, but he is surrounded by the corpses of Orcs much less fortunate than he.\n",
[10866]="70052796\n1\tTalk to Gultháva and follow her into the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah\tThe Maiden of the Gladden waits for you by the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah.\n",
[10867]="70052795\n1\tCatch up to the Maiden of the Gladden further to the west in Gladdenmere\tThe Maiden of the Gladden has reappeared further to the west along the path that runs through Gladdenmere.\n2\tTalk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden\tThe Maiden of the Gladden stares at you cryptically.\n3\tCatch up to the Maiden of the Gladden further to the west along the path through Gladdenmere\tThe Maiden of the Gladden has reappeared further along the western path through Gladdenmere.\n4\tTalk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden\tThe Maiden of the Gladden stares at you with enigmatic eyes.\n5\tPick up the soil of purity\tThe Maiden of the Gladden asked you to pick up the soil of purity and sprinkle it on flowers planted by her friends throughout the Vales of Anduin.\n6\tSprinkle soil of purity on Merillif's flower\030Sprinkle soil of purity on Braiglad's flower\030Sprinkle soil of purity on Silloth's flower\030Sprinkle soil of purity on Lenhwest's flower\030Defeat Orcs or goblins in the Vales of Anduin (total: 12)\tThe Maiden of the Gladden asked you to find the flowers planted by her long-lost friends throughout the Vales of the Anduin and sprinkle the soil of purity on them. You have marked the locations she gave to you on your map: Merillif's Flower grows within the camp of Lúlstrok. Braiglad's Flower grows behind a house in Waldfast. Silloth's Flower grows on the sloping path that climbs up through Brafulug. Lenhwest's Flower grows in the camp outside the cave of Fil Sulmog.\n7\tReturn to Gultháva near the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah\tThe Maiden of the Gladden waits for you by the flooded dwarf-hold of Kidzul-kâlah.\n",
[10868]="70052790\n1\tDefeat shades in the Gladden Fields (total: 10)\030Search Tol Send for Vagári the Wanderer\030Search Sharkey's Slough for Vagári the Wanderer\030Search Lúlstrok for Vagári the Wanderer\030Search Tûn Melen for Vagári the Wanderer\tGandalf has asked you to explore several locations in the Gladden Fields, defeating shades you find, and to search for Vagári the Wanderer.\n2\tYou feel a watchful presence to the west\tGandalf has asked you to explore several locations in the Gladden Fields, defeating shades you find, and to search for Vagári the Wanderer.\n3\tSearch for Vagári the Wanderer on the western side of the Gladden Fields\tYou felt something watching you from the western side of the Gladden Fields. Could it be the shade you seek?\n4\tTalk to the shade\tYou have found a watchful presence that seems to match Badwila's description of Vagári the Wanderer on the western side of the Gladden Fields.\n5\tThe shade of Vagári the Wanderer begins to fade from view\tThe shade of Vagári the Wanderer begins to fade from view.\n6\tSearch atop the cliff path to the north-west for the new presence\tYou felt another watchful presence up the cliff path to the north-west of where you encountered Vagári the Wanderer.\n7\tTalk to Gultháva, the Maiden of the Gladden\tThe Maiden of the Gladden stands by the rocky path in Gladdenmere, watching you carefully.\n",
[10869]="70052791\n1\tTalk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús and tell him of Badwila's frightening encounter\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús, studying the Black Book of Mordor.\n2\tTalk to Elrond outside the Beorninghús\tElrond is outside the Beorninghús.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús.\n",
[10870]="7003E2FF\n1\tDefeat shades in the western Fields of Fornost (total: 10)\tShades can be found in the western Fields of Fornost. You should defeat shades in the Fields of Fornost.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated many shades in the western Fields of Fornost.\n",
[10871]="7002C9EB\n1\tTalk to Wynstan at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\030Talk to Bagmund at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore\tWynstan and Bagmund are both at Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Aculf asked you to speak with both Wynstan and Bagmund and seek their opinions regarding what should be done about the shades.\n",
[10872]="70033047\n1\tDefeat Ghâsh-hai Orcs at Hadâd-mezer\tHadâd-mezer is located to the south-east of Anazârmekhem of Flaming Deeps. You should defeat Orcs in Hadâd-mezer.\n2\tDefeat Orcs at Hadâd-mezer (total: 8)\tHadâd-mezer is located to the south-east of Anazârmekhem of Flaming Deeps. You should defeat Orcs in Hadâd-mezer.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have successfully thinned the number of Orcs in Hadâd-mezer, making it much easier for dwarves of Anazârmekhem to get in and out of this area.\n",
[10873]="7006025A\n1\tEnter Tûr Fúar, the Drearspire\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should enter Tûr Fúar.\n2\tTalk to Múta inside the entrance of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Múta in Tûr Fúar.\n3\tSummon Múta to your side\tSummon Múta to your side.\n4\tDefeat Curcúan\030Defeat Lasairë\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should defeat Curcúan and Lasairë in Tûr Fúar.\n5\tDefeat Claghórd\030Summon Claghórd\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should defeat Claghórd in Tûr Fúar.\n6\tDefeat High Priestess Ásachal\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should defeat High Priestess Ásachal in Tûr Fúar.\n7\tTalk to Múta in Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Múta in Tûr Fúar.\n8\tTalk to Múta in the upper reaches of Tûr Fúar\tTûr Fúar, the Drearspire can be found at Agal Dûn. You should talk to Múta in the upper reaches of Tûr Fúar.\n",
[10874]="70000759\n1\tMeet Grimbriar's spy\tGrimbriar's spy will meet you by a grey rock in a stand of trees, north of Bree-town. Grimbriar has sent you to meet a spy he insinuated into the ranks of the brigands in hopes that he will reveal information about Sharkey and his plans.\n2\tTalk to Chief Watcher Grimbriar\tWatcher Grimbriar can be found at the stone house near the cross-roads outside of Bree. The spy's notes further supported the brigand's letter, verifying that Sharkey is no brigand himself, but an influential man of the south. Grimbriar must know.\n",
[10875]="70054C9F\n1\tDestroy abandoned fell beast eggs (total: 8)\tAbandoned fell beast eggs can be found within Gath Daeroval, the Shadow-roost. You should destroy any abandoned fell beast eggs that you find.\n2\tCompleted\tDestroyed many abandoned fell beast eggs.\n",
[10876]="70020C88\n1\tThe goat-herds graze the land to the west of Gavar Cadlus. Grufudh asked you to investigate the evil shadows he and his fellow goatherds saw among their herds. They only seem to come at night, but may be found elsewhere during the day.\t\n2\tDefeat Druggavar in the Windfells (total: 3)\tDruggavar have appeared among the herds of the Uch-lûth, west of Gavar Cadlus. Grufudh asked you to find a way to banish the Druggavar from their lands.\n3\tTalk to Grufudh at Gavar Cadlus\tGrufudh is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd.\n",
[10877]="70020C8B\n1\tDefeat Druggavar or wolves in the Windfells (total: 3)\tDruggavar haunt the lands to the west of Gavar Cadlus. Iuan has asked you to hunt down and banish the Druggavar of Enedwaith.\n2\tTalk to Iuan at Gavar Cadlus\tIuan is at Gavar Cadlus in the Windfells of Enedwaith, east of the goat-herd. You should return to Iuan with news of your victory.\n",
[10878]="70046BF8\n1\tPatrol the abandoned refuge of Thurindath\030Patrol the abandoned refuge of Adab Dolen\030Patrol the abandoned refuge of Torngroth\tThurindath can be found far to the south-east of Henneth Annûn, Adab Dolen can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn, and Torngroth can be found far to the north-west of Henneth Annûn. Mablung has asked you to scout the old Ranger refuges of Thurindath, Adab Dolen, and Torngroth. You should seek them out and take note of what you discover.\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tMablung can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. You have scouted the abandoned Ranger refuges and should now tell Mablung of what you discovered.\n",
[10879]="7002EF1C\n1\tDefeat mounted Orcs\t\n2\tDefeat mounted Orcs (total: 10)\tMounted Orcs can be found throughout the Entwash Vale. You should hunt the mounted Orcs patrolling the Entwash Vale.\n",
[10880]="7006C659\n1\tSearch three spots around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereabouts\tSearch the Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.\n2\tSearch around Esh-kimâkhi for clues as to Eshtali's whereabouts\tContinue searching Crypts of Esh-kimâkhi south of Urmâkh for signs of Mizâdi's missing husband, Eshtali. Mizâdi said he would be wearing crimson robes.\n3\tExamine the man to determine if he is Eshtali\tExamine the man to determine if he is Eshtali.\n4\tGive Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death\tGive Mizâdi in Urmâkh news of her husband's death.\n",
})
